        'intro' => 'Monona might be the easiest city on our map: it\'s a straight run across the Beltline from our south Madison shop, and the whole city fits between Lake Monona and the highway. We\'ve run jobs off Monona Drive, along Winnequah Road where the streets bend with the shoreline, and in the blocks behind the South Towne shopping district. 57 completed Monona jobs since 2021, and no two are ever far apart.',
        'localNotes' => [
            'What makes Monona distinct is how consistent the housing is. Almost the entire city went up in the post-war decades, so the standard Monona garage is a modest one-car or narrow two-car from the 1950s or 60s, sometimes widened since, often with hardware that has outlived several roofs. Original tracks with sixty winters on them, steel doors on their third spring set, openers older than the drivers they let out. It\'s honest, fixable equipment, and we\'d usually rather repair it than talk you into a new door, but when a panel from 1958 finally folds, we\'ll show you the math on both options.',
            'We\'re not a call center with a map. Twins Garage Doors is a family company run by twin brothers out of our Madison shop, and Monona is part of the regular route. There\'s a good chance we\'ve already worked on a door on your street.',
            'Living next to a lake is wonderful for most of the year and mildly corrosive for all of it. Lake Monona keeps the air here damper than a subdivision on a hilltop, and damp plus sixty-year-old steel plus a winter\'s worth of road salt off Monona Drive is how tracks pit, hinges seize, and cables fray from the inside out. On older Monona garages we always inspect the cables when we\'re in for anything else, because a rust-weakened cable doesn\'t give warnings, it just lets go.',
        ],
        'faq' => [
            ['q' => 'How much does it cost to repair a garage door in Monona?', 'a' => 'Most spring replacements land between $575 and $1,225 for the complete job, cable repairs between $325 and $625, and minor opener repairs between $100 and $300. Those ranges come from our own completed local jobs, 57 of them in Monona since 2021. You approve a flat quote before we start.'],
            ['q' => 'How quickly can a technician get to Monona?', 'a' => 'Same-day in most cases, and Monona is about as close to our shop as a city can get, straight across the Beltline. Call (608) 420-2377, tell us what the door is doing, and we\'ll give you an honest arrival window.'],
            ['q' => 'My garage door is from the 1960s. Can it still be repaired?', 'a' => 'Usually yes, and often for far less than a replacement. Springs, cables, rollers, and hinges for older doors are standard stock on our trucks. The honest exception is a failing wood or early steel panel, where we\'ll price the repair and the replacement side by side and let you pick.'],
            ['q' => 'Why do garage door cables rust faster near the lake?', 'a' => 'Damp lake air plus winter road salt accelerates corrosion on steel cables and tracks, and cables fail from the inside where you can\'t see it. On older Monona garages we inspect cables on every visit. A cable repair runs $325 to $625; a snapped cable with a car under the door costs more than money.'],
            ['q' => 'What can I do to maintain my garage door myself?', 'a' => 'Twice a year: lubricate rollers, hinges, and springs with garage door lube (not WD-40), rinse salt residue off the bottom seal and tracks in spring, and test the safety reverse with a scrap of wood. Leave spring and cable adjustments to us, or let a $49 tune-up cover the whole checklist.'],
        ],
    ],
    'cottage-grove' => [
        'label' => 'Cottage Grove',
        'metro' => 'madison',
        'completedJobs' => 14,
        'lat' => 43.0786,
        'lng' => -89.1998,
        'mapEmbedUrl' => 'https://www.google.com/maps?q=Cottage+Grove+WI&output=embed',
        'neighbors' => ['sun-prairie', 'monona', 'mcfarland', 'deerfield', 'madison', 'marshall'],
        'intro' => 'Cottage Grove sits just east of Madison where the Glacial Drumlin State Trail begins, and getting there is a quick hop on I-94 or County Road BB from our shop. We\'ve completed 48 jobs in the village since 2021, most of them in the family subdivisions that turned Cottage Grove from a crossroads into one of Dane County\'s steadiest commuter towns.',
        'localNotes' => [
            'Those subdivisions are the story here. The village grew in waves from the 1990s through the 2010s, so whole streets share the same door vintage: two- and three-car garages, builder-grade torsion springs, and openers installed the week the family moved in. Hardware like that ages by the calendar, and when one wave hits its cycle limit we\'ll often run two or three Cottage Grove calls in the same week, sometimes on the same street. The upside for you: we almost always have the right springs for your door already on the truck.',
            'We\'re not a call center with a map. Twins Garage Doors is a family company run by twin brothers out of our Madison shop, and Cottage Grove is part of the regular route. There\'s a good chance we\'ve already worked on a door on your street.',
            'Cottage Grove winters hit hardest at the bottom of the door. The flat, open ground east of the village lets snow drift and re-freeze against thresholds, and commuter households cycle their doors twice a day through the worst of it, packing slush into tracks that then set overnight like concrete. By February we see rollers grinding through ice ridges and bottom seals torn by re-freeze. A fall weatherstripping check and a $49 tune-up before the first deep freeze prevents most of what we get called for in the thaw.',
        ],
        'faq' => [
            ['q' => 'How much does it cost to repair a garage door in Cottage Grove?', 'a' => 'Most spring replacements land between $575 and $1,225 for the complete job, cable repairs between $325 and $625, and minor opener repairs between $100 and $300. Those ranges come from our own completed local jobs, 48 of them in Cottage Grove since 2021. Flat quote before any work starts.'],
            ['q' => 'How quickly can a technician get to Cottage Grove?', 'a' => 'Same-day in most cases. Cottage Grove is a short hop east on I-94 or County BB from our Madison shop. Call (608) 420-2377, describe what the door is doing, and we\'ll give you an honest arrival window for that day.'],
            ['q' => 'How do I open my garage door during a power outage?', 'a' => 'With the door fully closed, pull the red release cord and lift by hand. If the door feels far heavier than it should, stop: that\'s a broken spring carrying nothing, and the full door weight is on you. Openers with battery backup, standard on many new LiftMasters, skip this problem entirely.'],
            ['q' => 'My door is loud. Grinding, popping, rattling. Is that serious?', 'a' => 'It\'s the door asking for maintenance before it becomes a repair. Grinding usually means dry or worn rollers, popping can be a spring or loose hardware, rattling is often track bolts backing out. A $49 tune-up covers inspection and lubrication of all of it.'],
            ['q' => 'Do I really need an insulated garage door in Cottage Grove?', 'a' => 'If the garage is attached or you park a daily commuter in it, yes, it earns its keep. An insulated Clopay keeps the garage workable through a Wisconsin January, protects the opener\'s electronics from deep-freeze swings, and quiets the door. Most new doors we install here are insulated steel.'],
        ],
    ],
    'mount-horeb' => [
        'label' => 'Mount Horeb',
        'metro' => 'madison',
        'completedJobs' => 12,
