        'neighbors' => ['cottage-grove', 'marshall', 'sun-prairie', 'mcfarland', 'stoughton', 'madison'],
        'intro' => 'Deerfield sits out US 12 east of Madison, where Koshkonong Creek winds through farm country, and we\'ve been working its doors steadily: 36 completed Deerfield jobs since 2021. The village core along Main Street carries older homes with detached garages, and the newer streets on the village edge bring the standard modern package of attached two-car garages and builder hardware.',
        'localNotes' => [
            'What makes Deerfield calls different from a Madison subdivision run is everything behind the house. Out here the garage is often the smallest door we touch on the property: pole sheds, machine sheds, and workshop outbuildings carry big, heavy doors that work hard and get serviced rarely. We handle those alongside the house door, and a lot of Deerfield visits end up covering two or three doors once the homeowner remembers the shed door has been screeching since March.',
            'We\'re not a call center with a map. Twins Garage Doors is a family company run by twin brothers out of our Madison shop, and Deerfield is part of the regular route. There\'s a good chance we\'ve already worked on a door on your road.',
            'Detached garages and outbuildings dominate here, and they winter differently than an attached garage. No heat bleed from the house means the hardware cold-soaks to the full overnight temperature, and steel at twenty below is brittle steel. Springs, cables, and rollers in unheated Deerfield buildings fail earlier in the season and harder than their in-town cousins. If the shed door was stiff last February, this is the year to have it looked at in the fall instead.',
        ],
        'faq' => [
            ['q' => 'How much does it cost to repair a garage door in Deerfield?', 'a' => 'Most spring replacements land between $575 and $1,225 for the complete job, cable repairs between $325 and $625, and minor opener repairs between $100 and $300. Those ranges come from our own completed local jobs, 36 of them in Deerfield since 2021. Flat quote before any work starts.'],
            ['q' => 'How quickly can a technician get to Deerfield?', 'a' => 'Same-day in most cases. Deerfield is a straight run out US 12 from our Madison shop and pairs naturally with Cottage Grove and Marshall stops. Call (608) 420-2377 and we\'ll give you an honest arrival window.'],
            ['q' => 'Do you work on pole shed and outbuilding doors?', 'a' => 'Yes, regularly, and often on the same visit as the house door. Big shed doors use heavier hardware but the same physics: springs, cables, rollers, tracks. Tell us what you\'ve got when you call so the truck arrives stocked for both.'],
            ['q' => 'Why do unheated garage doors break more in winter?', 'a' => 'No heat bleed means the whole system cold-soaks to the overnight low, and spring steel gets brittle as it gets cold. Add stiff, unlubricated rollers and the opener works against the whole system. Most of our January Deerfield calls trace back to exactly this.'],
            ['q' => 'Do I need to replace both springs if only one broke?', 'a' => 'On a two-spring door, almost always yes. Both springs carry the same cycle count, so the survivor is near its own limit, and one combined visit is cheaper than two. That pairing is already reflected in the $575 to $1,225 whole-ticket range.'],
