            'River towns get river winters. Fog off the Sugar River and Lake Belle View settles on cold mornings and freezes where it lands, and a garage door is a big cold surface pointed at the weather. Frosted tracks grind rollers, iced seals tear when the door finally breaks free, and repeated frost-thaw cycles work moisture into hinge pins and cable strands. If your door sounds worse every winter morning than it did the night before, that\'s the frost cycle at work, and a proper lubrication and seal service interrupts it.',
