            ['q' => 'How quickly can a technician get to Belleville?', 'a' => 'Same-day in most cases. Belleville sits on our southern route down Highway 69, pairing with Verona and Oregon stops most weeks. Call (608) 420-2377 and we\'ll give you an honest arrival window for the day.'],
            ['q' => 'Why is my garage door so loud on winter mornings?', 'a' => 'Frost off the river and lake settles into tracks and rollers overnight, and dry, cold metal grinds until it warms. Proper garage door lubricant (not WD-40) on rollers, hinges, and springs quiets most of it. If the noise is a single loud bang, that was a spring. Stop and call.'],
            ['q' => 'Can I keep using a door with one broken spring?', 'a' => 'No. The remaining spring and the opener are carrying weight they weren\'t sized for, and the door can slam or fall. Park the car outside, keep kids away from the door, and call us. Spring replacement runs $575 to $1,225 for the complete job.'],
            ['q' => 'Do you cover the countryside around Belleville?', 'a' => 'Yes. The farms and rural homes between Belleville, Oregon, and Evansville are regular stops, outbuilding doors included. Same process everywhere: diagnosis in front of you, flat quote, work starts only after you approve it.'],
        ],
