        'intro' => 'Cross Plains is where the flat Madison basin runs into the Driftless hills, and the drive out US 14 past Middleton is one of the prettier runs on our schedule. The village stretches along the highway and Black Earth Creek, with the older homes down in the valley near Main Street and newer builds climbing the hillsides on either side.',
        'localNotes' => [
            'That geography is a garage door variable most towns don\'t have. Hillside driveways shed meltwater across their aprons all winter, and where it re-freezes overnight, doors seal themselves to the slab or grind their bottom rollers through ice. Valley lots along the creek hold cold and damp instead, which is slow but steady work on steel hardware. Between the two, Cross Plains doors earn their fall tune-up more than most, and we\'d rather adjust a seal in October than chip a door loose in January.',
