            'The cold pockets in the creek valley get a few degrees below what Madison reports, and a few degrees matters to tired spring steel. The morning the valley thermometer bottoms out is the morning tired springs across town let go with a bang. If your door has been lifting slower or landing harder this fall, that\'s the warning shot. Spring tension checked and corrected on your schedule beats a snapped spring on the coldest Monday of the year.',
