        'intro' => 'Edgerton sits right on I-90 halfway between Madison and Janesville, which makes it one of the easiest stops on our southeast run. The town made its name on tobacco warehouses, still celebrates Tobacco Heritage Days every summer, and its downtown along Fulton Street keeps the old brick to prove it. A few minutes east, the cottages and year-round homes around Lake Koshkonong add a completely different kind of garage to the route.',
        'localNotes' => [
            'Those two Edgertons wear out doors differently. In-town homes near Fulton Street are older stock, with garages added over the decades and hardware that has survived more winters than most roofs. The lake properties deal with humidity swings that in-town garages never see, plus long idle stretches when a seasonal place sits closed while the door hardware quietly rusts. First open of the spring is when lake-house doors fail, and we plan our April route accordingly.',
            'We\'re not a call center with a map. Twins Garage Doors is a family company run by twin brothers out of our Madison shop, and Edgerton is part of the regular I-90 route toward Janesville.',
            'Winter around Lake Koshkonong swings hard between damp and deep freeze, and that cycle is what kills door hardware here. Moisture works into cable strands and hinge pins during the mild spells, then the hard freeze locks it in and pries fibers and metal apart. In town, the classic Edgerton winter call is an older door whose seal froze to the slab and whose opener kept trying anyway. Either way, don\'t force it; a stripped opener gear turns a small fix into a bigger ticket.',
        ],
        'faq' => [
            ['q' => 'How much does it cost to repair a garage door in Edgerton?', 'a' => 'Most spring replacements land between $575 and $1,225 for the complete job, cable repairs between $325 and $625, and minor opener repairs between $100 and $300. Those ranges come from our own completed jobs across the Madison and Janesville area. Flat quote before work starts.'],
            ['q' => 'How quickly can a technician get to Edgerton?', 'a' => 'Same-day in most cases. Edgerton sits right on I-90 between our Madison shop and our Janesville stops, so it slots into the route most days. Call (608) 420-2377 for an honest arrival window.'],
            ['q' => 'My lake place\'s door won\'t open after sitting all winter. What happened?', 'a' => 'Months of idle damp followed by hard freeze: rusted cables, seized rollers, sometimes a spring that quietly failed with nobody home to hear the bang. Don\'t force it. We\'ll inspect the whole system and quote one flat number before touching anything.'],
            ['q' => 'Should I replace my door or keep repairing it?', 'a' => 'We quote the repair first, because the repair usually wins. When panels are failing or the hardware has been patched one time too many, we\'ll show both numbers side by side. A new insulated Clopay runs $2,625 to $4,400 installed, with GoodLeap monthly payments available.'],
            ['q' => 'What\'s the most common garage door repair you do around Edgerton?', 'a' => 'Springs, same as everywhere, but with a lake twist: humidity-shortened spring and cable life on Koshkonong-area properties. A spring replacement here runs $575 to $1,225 for the whole ticket, and we check the cables on every spring job as a matter of course.'],
