        'intro' => 'Evansville is the kind of town preservationists write about: block after block of Victorian and early-1900s homes in one of the area\'s larger historic districts, with Lake Leota Park anchoring the north side of town. We reach it down Highway 14 through Oregon, and it rounds out our southern loop with Belleville and the Janesville corridor.',
        'localNotes' => [
