            'Old detached garages take winter on the chin. No house heat, original single-pane windows if any, and framing that has settled for a century, so every freeze-thaw cycle racks the opening a little and the door binds where it didn\'t last year. Frost heave under a 1920s slab does the rest. The fix is rarely dramatic: track realignment, fresh rollers, spring tension matched to the door\'s real weight. But skipping it for a few winters is how a repairable door becomes a replacement.',
        ],
        'faq' => [
            ['q' => 'How much does it cost to repair a garage door in Evansville?', 'a' => 'Most spring replacements land between $575 and $1,225 for the complete job, cable repairs between $325 and $625, and minor opener repairs between $100 and $300. Those ranges come from our own completed jobs across the Madison area. You approve a flat quote before work starts.'],
            ['q' => 'How quickly can a technician get to Evansville?', 'a' => 'Same-day in most cases. Evansville anchors our southern loop down Highway 14 through Oregon. Call (608) 420-2377, tell us what the door is doing, and we\'ll give you an honest window for the day.'],
            ['q' => 'Can you put a modern door on a historic detached garage?', 'a' => 'Yes, and we do it carefully. We measure the real opening, deal honestly with settled framing and tight headroom, and pick a Clopay style that suits the house instead of fighting it. When the framing needs a carpenter first, we\'ll tell you straight.'],
            ['q' => 'Why does my old garage door bind in winter and free up in spring?', 'a' => 'Freeze-thaw racks settled framing and heaves old slabs, so the opening changes shape with the season. Track realignment and spring tension set for the door\'s true weight usually solve it. Left alone, the binding wears out rollers, cables, and eventually the opener.'],
            ['q' => 'Is one broken spring urgent if the door still opens?', 'a' => 'Yes. The opener and any surviving spring are lifting weight they weren\'t sized for, and the door can fall. Stop using it, keep people clear, and call us. With the $0 service call with repair, the diagnosis costs you nothing.'],
