        'intro' => 'Fort Atkinson sits where the Rock River bends through Jefferson County, a dairy-country town proud enough of that heritage to host the Hoard Historical Museum, with a working downtown along Main Street that most towns this size would trade for. We reach it on the Highway 26 corridor, the same run that takes us through Milton, and it marks the eastern edge of our Rock County loop.',
        'localNotes' => [
            'The housing follows the river and the decades. Older neighborhoods near downtown and Jones Park carry early-and-mid-1900s homes, many with detached garages built when cars were narrower and headroom was whatever the rafters allowed. Newer subdivisions along the Highway 26 bypass have the modern package: attached two- and three-car garages, insulated doors, and builder springs working through their 10,000 cycles. We carry stock for both on the same truck, because a Fort Atkinson day usually includes both.',
            'We\'re not a call center with a map. Twins Garage Doors is a family company run by twin brothers out of our Madison shop, and Fort Atkinson is part of the regular eastern route.',
            'River fog is the local winter signature. Cold mornings along the Rock put frost on everything within a few blocks of the water, and a garage door is the biggest frost collector on the property. Frozen seals, frosted tracks, and rollers that grind until mid-morning are the pattern, and doors that get forced through it pay in bent brackets and stripped opener gears. Add the salt spray zone along the Highway 26 bypass and hardware here earns its inspection. If your door sounds angriest before 9 am, that\'s the river talking.',
        ],
        'faq' => [
            ['q' => 'How much does it cost to repair a garage door in Fort Atkinson?', 'a' => 'Most spring replacements land between $575 and $1,225 for the complete job, cable repairs between $325 and $625, and minor opener repairs between $100 and $300. Those ranges come from our own completed jobs across the region. You approve a flat quote before work starts.'],
            ['q' => 'How quickly can a technician get to Fort Atkinson?', 'a' => 'Same-day in most cases. Fort Atkinson is the eastern stop on the Rock County loop we run through Milton on Highway 26. Call (608) 420-2377 and we\'ll give you an honest arrival window rather than a promise nobody can keep.'],
            ['q' => 'My door grinds every morning but is fine by noon. Do I need a repair?', 'a' => 'That\'s river frost in the tracks and rollers, and it\'s worth addressing before it becomes a repair. Forcing a frosted door strips opener gears and bends brackets. Fresh lubrication, seal service, and balanced springs usually end the morning fight.'],
            ['q' => 'How long do garage door springs last?', 'a' => 'Around 10,000 cycles, or 7 to 10 years for a typical household. Detached garages near the river age springs faster because cold, damp steel is brittle steel. If your springs are original to a 2000s build, have them checked this fall.'],
            ['q' => 'Can you replace just one panel instead of the whole door?', 'a' => 'Sometimes, if the model is still made and the rest of the door is sound. We\'ll price the panel against the door honestly. On older discontinued doors a matching panel often can\'t be had, and we\'ll tell you that up front instead of ordering the wrong thing.'],
        ],
    ],
    'marshall' => [
