        'neighbors' => ['sun-prairie', 'deerfield', 'cottage-grove', 'deforest', 'madison', 'mcfarland'],
        'intro' => 'Marshall sits on Highway 19 where the Maunesha River bends through town, northeast of Madison past Sun Prairie. It\'s a village of older homes near the river and the school, newer streets filling in at the edges, and plenty of rural properties in every direction where the garage shares a driveway with a machine shed.',
        'localNotes' => [
            'Older village homes here often have garages that were added or rebuilt decades after the house went up, which means openings that aren\'t quite square, headroom that\'s tighter than modern hardware expects, and doors that have been shimmed and adjusted by three generations of owners. That\'s not a complaint. It\'s honest work we\'re good at, and it\'s why we measure and diagnose in person instead of quoting sight unseen over the phone.',
            'We\'re not a call center with a map. Twins Garage Doors is a family company run by twin brothers out of our Madison shop, and Marshall folds into the same route that covers Sun Prairie and Deerfield. When you call, you\'re talking to the same company your neighbors down Highway 19 already use.',
            'River-valley frost is Marshall\'s particular winter flavor. Cold air settles along the Maunesha overnight, and doors near the river pick up heavy frost that older wood doors absorb like a sponge. A wood door that has swollen with winter moisture binds in its tracks and gains real weight, and the spring tension that was right in September is wrong by January. If your older door drags every winter and frees up every spring, that cycle is wearing parts out early, and it\'s correctable.',
        ],
        'faq' => [
            ['q' => 'How much does it cost to repair a garage door in Marshall?', 'a' => 'Most spring replacements land between $575 and $1,225 for the complete job, cable repairs between $325 and $625, and minor opener repairs between $100 and $300. Those ranges come from our own completed jobs across the Madison area. You approve a flat quote before work starts.'],
            ['q' => 'How quickly can a technician get to Marshall?', 'a' => 'Same-day in most cases. Marshall rides the Highway 19 route we already run through Sun Prairie, so it slots into most days easily. Call (608) 420-2377 and we\'ll give you an honest arrival window instead of a guess.'],
            ['q' => 'My old wood door sticks every winter. Can it be fixed or is it done?', 'a' => 'Often fixable: correcting spring tension for the door\'s real winter weight, easing the tracks, and sealing the wood buys years. When the panels themselves are failing, we\'ll quote repair and replacement side by side. A new insulated Clopay runs $2,625 to $4,400 installed.'],
            ['q' => 'Can you install a new door in an opening that isn\'t square?', 'a' => 'Yes, that\'s common in older Marshall garages. We measure the real opening, order the door to fit, and correct what the framing allows during installation. It\'s exactly why we quote after measuring in person, never off a phone estimate.'],
            ['q' => 'What maintenance actually matters for a rural door?', 'a' => 'Twice-yearly lubrication of springs, rollers, and hinges, a seal check before freeze-up, and a safety-reverse test. Dusty driveways and unheated buildings age hardware faster than town garages. A $49 tune-up covers the full checklist, house door and shed door alike.'],
        ],
    ],
    'milton' => [
        'label' => 'Milton',
        'metro' => 'madison',
