        'neighbors' => ['janesville', 'edgerton', 'fort-atkinson', 'evansville', 'stoughton', 'madison'],
        'intro' => 'Milton grew up as two towns, Milton and Milton Junction, and you can still read the seam in the street grid and the pair of old downtowns. It\'s the home of the Milton House, the National Historic Landmark that once hid travelers on the Underground Railroad, and it sits on our Rock County loop where Highways 26 and 59 cross, just north of Janesville.',
        'localNotes' => [
            'A town with two historic cores has plenty of older homes, and their garages carry the usual honest wear: hardware several owners old, openings that have settled, and doors balanced by feel sometime in the last century. The newer subdivisions between the old cores and along the Highway 26 bypass are standard modern fare, attached garages and builder-grade springs moving through their cycle count. We work both sides of that seam every time we\'re in town.',
            'We\'re not a call center with a map. Twins Garage Doors is a family company run by twin brothers out of our Madison shop, and Milton folds into the same Rock County route as Janesville and Edgerton.',
            'Milton sits in open Rock County farm country, and winter wind here doesn\'t ask permission. Northwest gusts drive snow across the fields and stack it against whatever faces them, and a north-facing door on the edge of town can spend February behind a drift that refreezes nightly into a ridge of ice. Doors that fight through that ridge wear bottom seals, bend bottom brackets, and strain openers. If your door faces the field side of town, keep the threshold clear and the seal fresh; it\'s the cheapest winter insurance there is.',
        ],
        'faq' => [
            ['q' => 'How much does it cost to repair a garage door in Milton?', 'a' => 'Most spring replacements land between $575 and $1,225 for the complete job, cable repairs between $325 and $625, and minor opener repairs between $100 and $300. Those ranges come from our own completed jobs across the Madison and Janesville area. Flat quote before any work starts.'],
            ['q' => 'How quickly can a technician get to Milton?', 'a' => 'Same-day in most cases. Milton rides our Rock County loop with Janesville and Edgerton, an easy run down I-90 and Highway 26. Call (608) 420-2377 and we\'ll give you an honest arrival window for the day.'],
            ['q' => 'Why does my door slam shut faster than it used to?', 'a' => 'Slamming means the springs are no longer carrying their share of the door\'s weight, from age, a partial failure, or lost tension. It\'s dangerous to people and hard on panels. Have the tension checked now; a full spring replacement runs $575 to $1,225 if the steel is done.'],
            ['q' => 'Can you match a new door to an older Milton home?', 'a' => 'Yes. Clopay\'s range includes panel designs and window styles that sit naturally on early-1900s homes, not just new construction. We measure in person, show you options against your house, and quote the real installed number, typically $2,625 to $4,400.'],
            ['q' => 'How do I open my garage door during a power outage?', 'a' => 'Close the door fully if it isn\'t already, pull the red release cord, and lift by hand. If it\'s suddenly far heavier than normal, stop: that\'s a spring failure, and the full door weight is on your back. Battery-backup LiftMaster openers avoid the problem entirely.'],
