    'prairie-du-sac' => [
        'label' => 'Prairie du Sac',
        'metro' => 'madison',
        'completedJobs' => null,  // no separable local job-count claim in the approved copy
        'lat' => 43.292,
        'lng' => -89.7222,
        'mapEmbedUrl' => 'https://www.google.com/maps?q=Prairie+du+Sac+WI&output=embed',
        'neighbors' => ['cross-plains', 'middleton', 'waunakee', 'deforest', 'madison', 'verona'],
        'intro' => 'Prairie du Sac lines the west bank of the Wisconsin River, twinned with Sauk City just downstream, famous for the bald eagles that winter over the open water below the dam and for Wollersheim Winery on the bluff across the river. We come up US 12 from Madison and swing over on Highway 78, and the Sauk Prairie towns mark the northwest corner of our regular map.',
        'localNotes' => [
            'River-town housing here runs in layers up from the water: older homes near Water Street and the original village grid, mid-century blocks behind them, and newer subdivisions climbing toward the bluffs. The older garages are the narrow, detached kind that predate two-car life, and the hillside builds trade that problem for driveways that turn into toboggan runs every January. Both kinds of properties keep us honest, and both fit the same flat-quote process.',
            'We\'re not a call center with a map. Twins Garage Doors is a family company run by twin brothers out of our Madison shop, and Sauk Prairie is part of the regular route northwest.',
            'The river valley funnels the wind here, and winter rides it. Gusts channeled along the Wisconsin River drive powder into every gap in an aging weatherseal, and the open water below the dam keeps the air damp enough to frost hardware on clear, cold nights, the same conditions that bring the eagles in. Damp frost plus wind-packed thresholds is a hard combination on older detached garages near the water. If your door sticks, screeches, or leaks snow by February, it\'s telling you which part gave up first.',
        ],
        'faq' => [
            ['q' => 'How much does it cost to repair a garage door in Prairie du Sac?', 'a' => 'Most spring replacements land between $575 and $1,225 for the complete job, cable repairs between $325 and $625, and minor opener repairs between $100 and $300. Those ranges come from our own completed jobs across the greater Madison area. Flat quote before any work starts.'],
            ['q' => 'How quickly can a technician get to Prairie du Sac?', 'a' => 'Same-day in most cases. The Sauk Prairie towns are a regular run up US 12 and Highway 78 from our Madison shop. Call (608) 420-2377, describe what the door is doing, and we\'ll give you an honest window for the day.'],
            ['q' => 'Do you serve Sauk City too?', 'a' => 'Yes, both sides of the Sauk Prairie community, plus the rural properties along US 12 and the river bluffs. Same techs, same flat-quote process, same $0 service call with repair.'],
            ['q' => 'Why does snow keep blowing in under my door?', 'a' => 'Valley wind finds worn bottom seals and stiffened side weatherstripping. Replacing the seal and squaring the door\'s contact with the slab closes the gap, and it protects the opener from fighting a threshold ice ridge later. It\'s one of the fastest, cheapest fixes we make.'],
            ['q' => 'Is a steep driveway a problem for a garage door?', 'a' => 'The door doesn\'t care about the slope, but the ice does. Hillside driveways shed meltwater across the apron, and overnight re-freeze can seal the door to the slab. A good bottom seal, a clear threshold, and correct opener force settings prevent the damage forcing it would cause.'],
        ],
    ],
    'milwaukee' => [
