        'neighbors' => ['wauwatosa', 'waukesha', 'new-berlin', 'milwaukee', 'greenfield', 'oak-creek'],
        'intro' => 'Brookfield is next door to our Wauwatosa office, a short run west on Capitol Drive or Bluemound, so a Brookfield call rarely waits long for a truck. Most people know the city by the Bluemound Corridor, the three-mile commercial stretch from Moorland Road to Barker Road anchored by Brookfield Square, but the work we do happens on the quiet streets behind it, in the subdivisions that fill the blocks north and south of the corridor and along Capitol Drive.',
        'localNotes' => [
            'Brookfield\'s housing stock is remarkably consistent, and that consistency is exactly what keeps us busy. The city filled in through the 1960s, 70s, and 80s with ranches, split-levels, and two-story colonials, including the brick ranches and colonials along the 124th Street corridor on the Tosa line, and nearly all of them came with attached two- and three-car garages wearing builder-grade hardware. Springs, rollers, and openers that were all installed in the same few years all reach the end of their cycle life in the same few years, which is why one Brookfield street can produce three spring calls in a winter. We also see the newer subdivision homes on larger lots, where taller insulated doors and side-mount openers change the parts list.',
            'We\'re not a call center with a map. Twins Garage Doors is a family company run by twin brothers, and Brookfield is served from our own Wauwatosa office with the same techs, the same pricing discipline, and the same guarantee that built our reputation in Madison.',
            'Winter in Brookfield is an attrition game against original hardware. A spring is rated in cycles, and a door that\'s opened four times a day since the Reagan administration has spent them; the deep-cold mornings, which run colder here than by the lake, are when the spent ones let go. The wide driveways and open lots that make Brookfield comfortable also give the wind room to work, drifting snow against three-car garage doors and refreezing meltwater at the threshold on every thaw. If your door is original to the house, or you don\'t know how old the springs are, that\'s precisely the door the $49 tune-up exists for: we inspect and lubricate everything and tell you honestly how much life is left.',
        ],
        'faq' => [
            ['q' => 'How much does it cost to repair a garage door in Brookfield?', 'a' => 'Most spring replacements land between $575 and $1,225 for the complete job, cable repairs between $325 and $625, and minor opener repairs between $100 and $300. Those ranges come from our own completed jobs, not a lead-gen site\'s national table. You approve a flat quote before work starts.'],
            ['q' => 'How quickly can a technician get to me in Brookfield?', 'a' => 'Same-day in most cases. Our metro office is on Burleigh Street in Wauwatosa, one suburb east, so Brookfield is one of our shortest metro runs. Call (414) 800-9271 and we\'ll give you an honest arrival window, not a number we invented.'],
            ['q' => 'Do I need to replace both springs if only one is broken?', 'a' => 'Usually yes, and it saves you money. Both springs have cycled the same number of times, so the survivor is close behind. On Brookfield\'s 1970s and 80s houses the springs are often original, which makes the pair replacement even more clearly the right call. Our $575 to $1,225 range covers the whole ticket.'],
            ['q' => 'What\'s the quietest garage door opener for a room over the garage?', 'a' => 'A belt-drive LiftMaster. Belt drives run far quieter than the chain units most Brookfield colonials came with, which matters when a bedroom or office sits above the garage. Installed, a new LiftMaster runs $775 to $1,400, and we program remotes, keypad, and the app before we leave.'],
            ['q' => 'How important is an insulated garage door in Brookfield?', 'a' => 'Important on an attached garage, which is nearly every garage in Brookfield. An insulated Clopay door takes the edge off a Wisconsin January, protects anything stored inside, and cuts the draft into rooms above and beside the garage. Most new doors we install here are insulated steel.'],
