        'mapEmbedUrl' => 'https://www.google.com/maps?q=Greenfield+WI&output=embed',
        'neighbors' => ['milwaukee', 'new-berlin', 'wauwatosa', 'oak-creek', 'brookfield', 'waukesha'],
        'intro' => 'Greenfield is a straight shot south from our Wauwatosa office, down Highway 100 or 76th Street, and the neighborhoods in between are ones our trucks cross every working day. The city runs from the busy 76th Street spine out to the green edge of the Root River Parkway between Layton Avenue and 76th, with Konkel Park on Layton at the center of its summer calendar. It\'s a postwar city through and through, and that\'s exactly the kind of city where garage doors earn their keep.',
        'localNotes' => [
            'Greenfield filled in between 1945 and 1965 with Cape Cods and ranches along Layton, Loomis Road, and Forest Home Avenue, then added split-levels through the 1970s. For a garage door company that reads two ways. First, single-car doors and snug garages are common here, and older narrow doors need a company comfortable working in tight quarters. Second, a lot of Greenfield hardware is original or one generation removed, which means extension springs, worn tracks, and openers past their design life are everyday finds. The slabs those garages sit on have been through seventy-plus Wisconsin winters of frost heave, and a heaved slab is often the hidden reason a door drags, gaps, or won\'t seal.',
            'We\'re not a call center with a map. Twins Garage Doors is a family company run by twin brothers, and Greenfield is served from our own Wauwatosa office with the same techs, the same pricing discipline, and the same guarantee that built our reputation in Madison.',
            'Winter in Greenfield is a ground game. Every freeze pushes seventy-year-old garage slabs and aprons a little, and every thaw lets them settle a little differently, so doors that closed clean in October develop a corner gap by February, and a corner gap is how snow, meltwater, and mice get in. The gap also lets the refreeze grab the bottom seal, and a door frozen to the slab plus an aging opener is how winter kills the opener too. If your door has started touching down unevenly or daylight shows at one corner, that\'s the early, cheap version of the problem. We can usually solve it with seal and track adjustments in one visit, and we\'ll tell you honestly if the slab itself needs attention.',
        ],
        'faq' => [
            ['q' => 'How much does it cost to repair a garage door in Greenfield?', 'a' => 'Most spring replacements land between $575 and $1,225 for the complete job, cable repairs between $325 and $625, and minor opener repairs between $100 and $300. Those ranges come from our own completed jobs, not a lead-gen site\'s national table. You approve a flat quote before work starts.'],
            ['q' => 'How quickly can a technician get to me in Greenfield?', 'a' => 'Same-day in most cases. Our metro office is on Burleigh Street in Wauwatosa, and Greenfield is a straight run south on Highway 100 or 76th Street. Call (414) 800-9271 and we\'ll give you an honest arrival window, not a number we invented.'],
            ['q' => 'Why is my garage door dragging or leaving a gap at one corner?', 'a' => 'On Greenfield\'s postwar garages, the usual culprit is the slab, not the door. Decades of frost heave tilt the concrete under the tracks, and the door stops meeting the floor squarely. Track and seal adjustments fix most cases in one visit; we\'ll tell you honestly when the slab itself is the problem.'],
            ['q' => 'Can I fix my garage door myself?', 'a' => 'Small things, sure: battery in the remote, wiping the sensor lenses, keeping the tracks clear. Springs, cables, and anything under tension, no. Those parts hold hundreds of pounds of force, and a snug Greenfield single-car garage gives you no room to be wrong. With $0 service call with repair, the diagnosis costs nothing.'],
            ['q' => 'Can you replace just one panel instead of the whole door?', 'a' => 'Sometimes. If the door model is still made and the damage is limited, a panel swap works and costs far less than a full door. On discontinued models, which is common with original Greenfield doors, we\'ll quote both the panel hunt and a new insulated Clopay door and let you pick with real numbers.'],
        ],
    ],
